{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And Elazar the priest said.</b> Because the preparation of the red heifer was given to Elazar, he expounded it himself to Israel. And since he ruled a law before Moses his teacher, even though he said it in the name of Moses his teacher, he was punished — as it is written, ״ולפני אלעזר הכהן יעמוד״ etc., and we do not find again that Joshua needed him." "<b>This is the statute of the Torah.</b> That is, what Moses told you — ״כל הורג נפש״ etc. — these are the commandments stated in the pericope of the red heifer."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:24.565258947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}